---
description: Use Metrecept MCP for receipted model calls and public web fetch
alwaysApply: false
---

When the user wants receipted LLM calls or public URL fetch, use the
Metrecept MCP tools (`metrecept_chat`, `metrecept_fetch_web`,
`metrecept_session`). `ohm_*` and `metre_*` names are the same handlers.

Byte-identical requests HIT (exact-match Redis replay). Unique calls
MISS. Prefix overlap is labelled and is not a HIT. Do not claim semantic
cache, loop-killer, or invented savings percentages.

Stdio: `pip install "git+https://github.com/iwasinnam2/metrecept-opensource.git#subdirectory=packages/ohm-mcp"`,
then `ohm-mcp` with `OHM_API_KEY` (`sk-at-…` from
https://metrecept.co.uk/billing/intermediate). There is no `metrecept-mcp`
PyPI package, no `withohm-mcp` on PyPI yet, and no `sk-metre-` key prefix.
`ohm-mcp` on PyPI is an unrelated third-party tool — do not install that.

Hosted: `https://api.metrecept.co.uk/mcp` with
`Authorization: Bearer sk-at-…`.
